    "submission_date": "2021-08-27",
    "abstract": "Position methods such as sinusoidal and rotary embeddings fail to extrapolate to sequences longer than those seen in training. ALiBi removes position embeddings and instead adds a static, head-specific linear penalty proportional to query-key distance to attention scores. A 1.3B model trained on 1024 tokens extrapolates to 2048 with the perplexity of a sinusoidal model trained on 2048, while training faster and using less memory.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "Sinusoidal, rotary and T5-bias position methods extrapolate poorly or expensively beyond the training length.",
      "Adding -m (i - j) biases to attention scores, with no position embeddings, enables extrapolation.",
      "A 1.3B ALiBi model trained with L=1024 matches a sinusoidal model trained with L=2048 at evaluation length 2048, training 11% faster with 11% less memory.",
      "ALiBi's slopes are a fixed geometric sequence and need no tuning across datasets."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
